preConditionHook:
// THE ATOMIC OUTSIDE BAR. The bar lag bars ago engulfs the bar before it: its
// high reaches at or beyond the prior high and its low at or beyond the prior
// low, with an optional tick tolerance that admits Brooks's NEAR-outside bar
// (V16-06, toleranceTicks = 1).
//
// EL: high[lag] >= high[lag + 1] - toleranceTicks * tickSize and
//     low[lag] <= low[lag + 1] + toleranceTicks * tickSize and
//     (high[lag] > high[lag + 1] or low[lag] < low[lag + 1])
//
// THE STRICT-ON-ONE-SIDE TERM IS LOAD-BEARING. R00-04 and V00-05 state both
// sides inclusively, which lets a bar with exactly the prior bar's high and low
// be inside AND outside at the same time; T00-05 and T07-01 require the bar to
// reach strictly beyond on at least one side, and that reading won the merge.
// The inclusive-both form is what rows/01_bar.md recorded as the shape an
// atomic OutsideBar should use; the extra disjunct only removes the degenerate
// identical-range bar, and at toleranceTicks = 0 nothing else changes.
//
// Not LargeOutsideBar, which is this relation ANDed with a range at least
// largeMultiple x the mean bar range and has no tolerance (its largeMultiple is
// a size multiple, so 0 is outside any sane grid). Not OutsideBarInMidRange
// (the same relation plus a position band inside a 20-bar block), not
// OutsideBarWithoutPriorSignalBar (plus a negated signal bar), not
// OutsideBarCounterTrend (plus the always-in direction), and not
// OutsideOutsidePattern (two nested engulfs). Each of those inlines the
// relation because no atomic rule carried it; this is that rule.
//
// DIRECTION comes from the breakout of the pattern and from the body sign the
// pane supplies, so both sides are identical text -- the merge absorbed the
// directional variants T07-34, R00-06 and T21-68 for exactly that reason.
//
// The tick is written division-first, mirroring EL's MinMove / PriceScale, and
// read once per bar into a local since both are per-symbol constants. Every
// scratch value is a localVariables entry, never a hook-scope declaration, so
// the hooks survive a double placement. Deepest bar touched: lag + 1.
tickSize = ctx.MinMove() / ctx.PriceScale();
